{"metadata":{"externalID":"Systems","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"role":"collection","title":"Systems"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"]},{"title":"System Parameters","anchor":"System-Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"]},{"title":"Building and Running Schedules","anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"]},{"title":"Main-Actor Systems","anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"]},{"title":"Built-In Systems","anchor":"Built-In-Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"]},{"title":"Profiling","anchor":"Profiling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"schedule","type":"text"}]},{"text":" lists the systems of one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:"}]},{"code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Declare a System","anchor":"Declare-a-System"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the "},{"code":"@System","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro and give it a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update"},{"type":"text","text":" writes components, a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them, and a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it by its velocity:"}]},{"code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for you: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gravity"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Movement"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"type":"text","text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also conform a type to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"reference"},{"text":" by hand and write its ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" method, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives the whole world. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"reference"},{"text":" for when to do that.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Run Systems in a Schedule","anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"reference"},{"text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" require one system to run after or before another; "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and "},{"code":"runIf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" skips"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" finds those pairs so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test can keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"]}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"System()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"title":"Schedule"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduleBuilder":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","abstract":[{"text":"A result builder that collects the systems written in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"},{"text":"’s closure.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"ScheduleBuilder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulebuilder","role":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each."}],"title":"Query"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order satisfies them all.","type":"text"}],"title":"CyclicOrdering"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardEvents":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each event of one type to an asynchronous stream, so code outside the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule can await the events.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"ForwardEvents","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardevents","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","kind":"symbol","title":"SystemProfile","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardChanges","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardChanges","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity.","type":"text"}],"title":"ForwardChanges"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemSet"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemSet"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"title":"SystemSet"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ambiguities"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV","text":"Ambiguity"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"orders.","type":"text"}],"title":"ambiguities()"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system together with the ordering constraints, sets and conditions a schedule runs it with."}],"title":"ScheduledSystem"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"title":"access","required":true,"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if it may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change anything."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"access","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV","text":"Access","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","defaultImplementations":1},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainActorSystem"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","kind":"symbol","title":"MainActorSystem","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainActorSystem"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Update"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventReader":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":